From f35d1b753306d1aa6110f7c657aa21efa491bc99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Dowell <mbd06b+github@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:45:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: `brit log` takes revisions and ranges; `diff tree
 --name-only`

Agents fell back to Git for two daily questions: "which commits are on
`origin/dev` and not here" and "which files changed since the merge base".

`brit log` read every positional argument as a path and refused it, so
`brit log origin/dev` and `brit log A..B` could not be used at all. It now
takes revisions before `--`: `A`, `^A`, `A..B`, `A...B`, `A^@` and `A^!`,
combinable and limited by `-n`. Commits are selected and ordered like
`git rev-list --date-order`, the order plain `brit log` already used. A
literal path after `--` keeps its existing refusal. The topological walk
queues tips before applying ends, so a tip that is itself excluded
(`HEAD..HEAD`) is dropped first.

`diff tree` gains `--name-only` (paths like
`git diff --name-only --no-renames`, quoted under `core.quotePath`; a rename
is its deleted and added path, a gitlink its path), `--merge-base A B`, and
one-argument `A..B` / `A...B` forms. The endpoint forms apply to the
existing object and `--stat` outputs too.

Oracles: `revision_ranges::log_lists_revisions_and_ranges_like_rev_list_date_order`
and `diff_name_only::name_only_lists_changed_paths_for_two_trees_ranges_and_merge_bases`
compare with stock Git on skewed-date merges, unrelated roots, annotated tags,
byte-order neighbours of `/`, renames, non-ASCII names and a gitlink. On the
elohim monorepo, `origin/main..origin/dev` (11457 commits) and
`origin/main...origin/dev` (26659 paths) matched Git byte for byte.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
